# Church Intelligence Audio Console

## Collective Master Implementation Blueprint

**Status:** Consolidated product and engineering blueprint  
**Purpose:** Define what the product should become, how its parts fit together, and the order in which it should be implemented.  
**Architecture principle:** One hardware-aware audio platform, one authoritative signal graph, one real-time engine, and thirteen synchronized workspaces.

---

## 1. Product definition

Church Intelligence Audio Console is a professional digital mixing and audio engineering platform for church sound systems. It brings live mixing, computer-side processing, routing, measurement, broadcast, diagnostics, presets, and guided recommendations into one coherent control room. Its architecture is benchmarked against high-capacity digital consoles and must not be designed around entry-level mixer or PC sound-card limits.

The product must work across analog, digital, and hybrid installations through capability-aware device integrations. The Yamaha MG16XU and ASUS Xonar DGX are the first reference setup for development and validation; they are not the product's architectural limit.

### Product mission

Help church operators and audio engineers understand, operate, measure, and improve the sound system from source to destination, while clearly showing what the software can control, what it can observe, and what requires physical action.

### Core promise

**One engine. Any supported hardware. Complete signal visibility. Intelligent sound management.**

### Primary users

- **Service operator:** runs the live mix, monitors outputs, and needs quick access to safe controls.
- **Audio engineer:** configures processing, routing, speakers, measurements, and system profiles.
- **System maintainer:** diagnoses devices, failures, signal loss, and configuration drift.

The same installation may have one person performing all three roles.

