## 12. Implementation roadmap and release gates

Build the shared engine foundation before advanced intelligence. Each phase ends with evidence that its exit criteria work on the reference system and a simulated profile. This blueprint defines acceptance criteria; no implementation or test execution is claimed here.

| Phase | Deliverable | Exit criteria |
|---|---|---|
| **0. Architecture and capability inventory** | Confirm target OS/runtime, professional I/O/networking roadmap, driver APIs, clocks, safety path, capacity target, graph contracts, permissions, and lab profiles | Verified capability inventory; selected multichannel pro interface for qualification; documented topology; agreed engine/UI boundary |
| **1. Device I/O and engine lifecycle** | Device discovery, pro-driver host, format negotiation, capture/playback, start/stop, disconnect/reconnect, diagnostics | Correct devices/formats reported; safe start/stop and recovery; stable multichannel signal on the qualified pro interface |
| **2. Signal Graph and transactions** | Typed nodes/edges, channel maps, validation, versioning, apply/rollback | Reject invalid channel maps/cycles; active graph matches engine execution |
| **3. Metering and Signal Journey** | Measurement taps, event stream, forward/reverse trace, global search | Measurements identify point/source/version; branching routes trace correctly; stale traces detected |
| **4. Core mixing and DSP** | Channels, buses, faders, sends, EQ, dynamics, delay, meters | Audio persists through UI navigation; real-time constraints hold; controls affect actual software engine state |
| **5. Virtual DI and instrument workflows** | Isolated-source routing, bass chain, source intelligence | Dry/processed route is explicit; no unintended duplicate feed; source-specific measurements verified |
| **6. Output, crossover, and speaker management** | Output mapping, speaker groups, crossover, delay, polarity, limiter | Only supported outputs exposed; verified routing and safe protection configuration |
| **7. Livestream and recording** | Independent broadcast/record buses, processing, monitoring, status | Broadcast path remains distinct where configured; correct meters and destinations shown |
| **8. Feedback and room intelligence** | Feedback analysis, measurement sessions, acoustic tools | Findings show evidence and measurement limits; no silent live corrections |
| **9. AI Sound Engineer** | Grounded analysis, explainable proposals, approval and audit | AI cannot bypass validation/permissions; AI unavailability does not interrupt audio |
| **10. Sound check, presets, diagnostics** | Guided checks, scene versioning/diff/apply, recovery | Check results distinguish measured/manual/not-testable; scene apply validates/rolls back |
| **11. Compatibility expansion and production hardening** | More adapters/profiles, stress/recovery review, documented bypass/failover path, usability polish | Release gates met for each supported device profile; failover tested where claimed; unsupported capabilities remain explicit |

The first implementation milestone is **Phase 0 followed by Phase 1**. Design/UI mockups may proceed in parallel only when they label illustrative values and do not imply unsupported controls.

