## 14. Decisions consolidated from the supplied notes

1. The product is universal-first; MG16XU/Xonar DGX are a reference profile.
2. One Unified Audio Engine executes audio, and one shared Signal Graph describes routes.
3. The three global system screens sit above the thirteen specialist workspaces.
4. Thirteen workspaces are grouped into six main navigation destinations.
5. The interface is a professional virtual console, not a generic admin dashboard.
6. Hardware, software, monitoring, estimates, and AI recommendations are visibly distinct.
7. Signal Journey is global, bidirectional, branch-aware, and generated from the active graph.
8. AI observes and recommends; the engine validates and applies only authorized commands.
9. Independent channel processing and scalable channel counts are architectural requirements.
10. The audio engine remains operational without UI, database, network, or AI availability.
11. Physical and virtual DI pathways share a software bass workspace but retain their electrical distinction.
12. EQ, crossover, speaker processing, and independent broadcast mixes are core platform capabilities.

